{"name":"Wizardcore","title":"Wizardcore","revision":234862,"url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Wizardcore","retrieved":"2026-09-06","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://www.fandom.com/licensing","language":"en","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Wizardcore is an aesthetic based off of magic, fantasy, and the taste for discovery and exploration. It's similar to Witchcore, with the same theme of magic, but is generally the more masculine counterpart. It is also related to the Academia aesthetics, with the need for knowledge and experimentation, whether it be of interests or projects."},{"kind":"heading","text":"History"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Wizardcore has its roots in folklore and mythology surrounding magicians in various cultures in the world. For example, the mythical magician Merlin was depicted in the legend of King Arthur."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"In the 20th century, wizards began to be associated with the fantasy genre of fiction. Wizards were often seen as the antagonists in a genre of Pulp Magazines called Sword and Sorcery. This continued into the boom of fantasy fiction from the 1960s to the 1980s, largely based on the popularization of The Lord of the Rings by J. R. R. Tolkien. These depictions of wizards often featured them with large cloaks and pointed hats surrounded by magic and energy, which is related to the \"Wizardposting\" meme."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"In the 1990s, the depictions of wizards started to change to be toned down and less archetypical. For example, the Harry Potter series depicted wizards as ordinary people."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Visuals"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Visuals that are part of Wizardcore but not limited to:"},{"kind":"list","text":"Wizard staffs (Commissioned or made yourself)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Walking sticks"},{"kind":"list","text":"Books (commonly leather-bound, old, and/or tattered)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cloaks and robes"},{"kind":"list","text":"Glass baubles and trinkets"},{"kind":"list","text":"Maps and blueprints (commonly older and weathered)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Old/Victorian mirrors"},{"kind":"list","text":"Succulents"},{"kind":"list","text":"Gems and stones"},{"kind":"list","text":"Brooches"},{"kind":"list","text":"Scrolls"},{"kind":"list","text":"Candles"},{"kind":"list","text":"Notebooks"},{"kind":"list","text":"Rustic items"},{"kind":"list","text":"Books"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Fashion"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The fashion of the Wizardcore aesthetic tends to be fantastical due to wizards being depicted as wise but eccentric in media."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Tops"},{"kind":"list","text":"Robes"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Bottoms"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ankle-length skirts"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Footwear"},{"kind":"list","text":"Boots"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Accessories"},{"kind":"list","text":"Pointed hats"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cloaks and capes"},{"kind":"list","text":"Scarfs"},{"kind":"list","text":"Belts with pouches"},{"kind":"list","text":"Shawls"},{"kind":"list","text":"Trench coats"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Activities"},{"kind":"list","text":"Potion-making (be it cocktails or chemistry)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Hanging out with your familiar (animal companion)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Studying spells"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Media"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Literature"},{"kind":"list","text":"Simon Snow series by Gemma T. Leslie"},{"kind":"list","text":"Harry Potter series"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Hobbit by J.R.R. Tolkien"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Lord of the Rings by J.R.R. Tolkien"},{"kind":"list","text":"Wizardology: The Book of the Secrets of Merlin by Dugald Steer"},{"kind":"list","text":"Discworld - Wizards sub-series"},{"kind":"list","text":"Young Wizards by Diane Duane"},{"kind":"list","text":"Earthsea by Ursula K. le Guin"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Wizards of Once by Cressida Crowell"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Dark is Rising by Susan Cooper"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Wheel of Time by Robert Jordan"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Black Mage by Daniel Barnes"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Video Games"},{"kind":"list","text":"Dungeons and Dragons"},{"kind":"list","text":"Pathfinder Roleplaying Game"},{"kind":"list","text":"Potion Craft: Alchemist Simulator by tinyBuild Games"},{"kind":"list","text":"Wizard101 by KingsIsle Entertainment"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mage Arena"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mages of Mystralia"},{"kind":"list","text":"Avencast: Rise of the Mage"},{"kind":"list","text":"Spells and Sercrets"},{"kind":"list","text":"Nox"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Television"},{"kind":"list","text":"Wizards of Waverly Place (2007-2012)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Merlin (2008-2012)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Magicians (2015-2020)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Wizards: Tales of Arcadia (2020)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Reign of the Seven Spellblades (2023)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Movies"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Sword in the Stone (1963)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Lord of the Rings trilogy (2001-2003)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Harry Potter (2001-2011)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Sorcerer's Apprentice (2010)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Characters"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Fictional wizards, people who use or practice magic derived from supernatural, occult, or arcane sources."},{"kind":"list","text":"Alex Russo (Wizards Of Waverly Place)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Zatanna (DC Universe)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ice King (Adventure Time)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Forest Wizard (Adventure Time)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Kyle (Fanboy and ChumChum)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Bufo (Adventure Time)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Harry Potter (Harry Potter franchise)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ron Weasley (Harry Potter franchise)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Doctor Strange (Marvel Cinematic Universe)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Max Russo (Wizards Of Waverly Place)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Haruto Sohma (Kamen Rider Wizard)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Majisto (Lego/Lego Dragon Masters)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Rincewind (Discworld)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Eskarina Smith (Discworld)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Yen Sid (Fantasia)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Balthazar Blake (The Sorcerer's Apprentice)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Gale (Baldur's Gate 3)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ziggy (Brawl Stars)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Shaman (ENA: Dream BBQ)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Harry Dresden (The Dresden Files)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cedric the Sorcerer (Sofia the First)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Miriel (Fire Emblem)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Marcia Overstrand (Septimius Heap)"}],"contentStatus":"full-source","images":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/a/a4/Wizardcore1.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20210120031057","caption":"Wizardcore1","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:Wizardcore1.jpg","remote":true,"local":"images/detail/1101-1.webp","localAvailable":true},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/2/2b/Wizard_Frog_From_Adventure_Time.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20230814100112","caption":"Bufo (Adventure Time)","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:Wizard_Frog_From_Adventure_Time.jpg","remote":true,"local":"images/detail/1101-2.webp","localAvailable":true}]}